<title>GERMANY: Opel says to interrupt German Vectra production.</title>
<headline>Opel says to interrupt German Vectra production.</headline>
<dateline>RUESSELSHEIM, Germany 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Adam Opel AG, a unit of General Motors, said on Wednesday it would interrupt Vectra production at its Ruesselsheim plant from Friday because of transport strikes in Spain.</p>
<p>The company said Vectra production would cease on Friday and through next week because of insufficient access to Vectra vehicle parts.</p>
<p>Output at other plants in Bochum, Eisenach and Kaiserslautern would not be affected, Opel said.  </p>
<p>Opel added that a flexible working hours agreement with its works council meant that it could balance out the missing work hours at a later stage.</p>
<p>The week-long strike by Spanish truck drivers has spread to almost all of northern Spain and hundreds of trucks are blocking main roads.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
